 in the blank: She is ____ honest woman.\",\"options\":[\"the\",\"a\",\"an\",\"no article\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is an honest woman.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He did not (B) knew the answer (C) to the last (D) question.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"After ‘did not’ use the base form: ‘know’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘under the weather’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"slightly ill\",\"out in the rain\",\"very happy\",\"worried about the news\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘under the weather’ means: slightly ill.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: An animal that eats only plants\",\"options\":[\"herbivore\",\"insectivore\",\"omnivore\",\"carnivore\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"An animal that eats only plants: herbivore.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘CORDIAL’.\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"careful\",\"central\",\"cordless\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘cordial’ means warm.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘EMINENT’.\",\"options\":[\"empty\",\"unknown\",\"imminent\",\"distinguished\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘eminent’ means distinguished; its opposite is ‘unknown’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He is senior ____ me by two years.\",\"options\":[\"than\",\"over\",\"from\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He is senior to me by two years.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) I am (B) looking forward (C) to see you (D) soon.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘Looking forward to seeing’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘keep your chin up’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"look at the sky\",\"sit straight\",\"stay positive in difficulty\",\"be proud\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘keep your chin up’ means: stay positive in difficulty.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who does not believe in God\",\"options\":[\"pilgrim\",\"atheist\",\"priest\",\"theist\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who does not believe in God: atheist.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LETHARGIC’.\",\"options\":[\"literal\",\"sluggish\",\"legal\",\"lethal\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘AUGMENT’.\",\"options\":[\"reduce\",\"decorate\",\"increase\",\"observe\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘augment’ means increase; its opposite is ‘reduce’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He apologised ____ being late.\",\"options\":[\"for\",\"about\",\"on\",\"of\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He apologised for being late.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He is (B) an honest (C) and hardworking (D) man.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":4,\"correctOption\":4,\"explanation\":\"The sentence is correct.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2025-06-18 02:00:00','2025-06-18 03:00:00'),('0c12b07b-8bb5-4282-87ea-e87d3e787e15','72213566-2c52-4e3d-9fbd-8e841e9040cc','7d5c7697-dfff-4207-a6e1-4861e7a15759','2026-03-31 10:00:00','2026-11-24 19:37:42','2026-03-31 10:26:00',NULL,'2026-03-31 10:00:00',2,0,NULL,35.00,60,'{\"q31\":{\"option\":0},\"q30\":{\"option\":2},\"q33\":{\"option\":1},\"q32\":{\"option\":1},\"q35\":{\"option\":2},\"q34\":{\"option\":1},\"q37\":{\"option\":0},\"q36\":{\"option\":2},\"q39\":{\"option\":3},\"q38\":{\"option\":1},\"q40\":{\"option\":3},\"q42\":{\"option\":1},\"q41\":{\"option\":2},\"q44\":{\"option\":2},\"q43\":{\"option\":1},\"q46\":{\"option\":2},\"q45\":{\"option\":0},\"q47\":{\"option\":1},\"q49\":{\"option\":2},\"q51\":{\"option\":0},\"q53\":{\"option\":0},\"q52\":{\"option\":0},\"q11\":{\"option\":2},\"q10\":{\"option\":3},\"q54\":{\"option\":3},\"q13\":{\"option\":2},\"q12\":{\"option\":3},\"q56\":{\"option\":1},\"q15\":{\"option\":2},\"q59\":{\"option\":0},\"q14\":{\"option\":2},\"q58\":{\"option\":3},\"q17\":{\"option\":0},\"q16\":{\"option\":1},\"q18\":{\"option\":2},\"q2\":{\"option\":3},\"q3\":{\"option\":1},\"q4\":{\"option\":0},\"q5\":{\"option\":2},\"q6\":{\"option\":2},\"q7\":{\"option\":3},\"q8\":{\"option\":3},\"q9\":{\"option\":1},\"q60\":{\"option\":2},\"q20\":{\"option\":2},\"q22\":{\"option\":3},\"q21\":{\"option\":1},\"q24\":{\"option\":2},\"q23\":{\"option\":1},\"q26\":{\"option\":3},\"q25\":{\"option\":3},\"q28\":{\"option\":3},\"q27\":{\"option\":2},\"q29\":{\"option\":2}}',NULL,'{\"attemptId\":\"0c12b07b-8bb5-4282-87ea-e87d3e787e15\",\"testId\":\"72213566-2c52-4e3d-9fbd-8e841e9040cc\",\"title\":\"HCLTech style · Aptitude + Computer basics\",\"companyTag\":\"HCLTech\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:42Z\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:42.352458576Z\",\"timeTakenSeconds\":0,\"score\":35,\"maxScore\":60,\"percent\":58,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Quantitative\",\"score\":9,\"max\":15,\"correct\":9,\"total\":15},{\"name\":\"Logical\",\"score\":6,\"max\":15,\"correct\":6,\"total\":15},{\"name\":\"Verbal\",\"score\":11,\"max\":15,\"correct\":11,\"total\":15},{\"name\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"score\":9,\"max\":15,\"correct\":9,\"total\":15}],\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"If 6x + 21 = 99, what is x?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"11\",\"12\",\"13\"],\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"6x = 78, so x = 13.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"A can finish a work in 20 days and B in 40 days. In how many days will they finish it working together?\",\"options\":[\"30 days\",\"77/6 days\",\"43/3 days\",\"40/3 days\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Together per day: 1/20 + 1/40 = 3/40; time = 40/3 days.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"What is the smaller angle between the hour and minute hands of a clock at 2:50?\",\"options\":[\"215°\",\"145°\",\"240°\",\"150°\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |60 − 275| = 145°.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"A train 120 m long passes a pole in 9 seconds. What is its speed in km/h?\",\"options\":[\"48 km/h\",\"40/3 km/h\",\"44 km/h\",\"54 km/h\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"120/9 m/s × 18/5 = 48 km/h.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"A rectangular field is 38 m long and 15 m wide. What is the cost of fencing it at Rs 15 per metre?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 1740\",\"Rs 8550\",\"Rs 1590\",\"Rs 795\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Perimeter = 2(38+15) = 106 m; cost = 106 × 15 = Rs 1590.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"What is the smaller angle between the hour and minute hands of a clock at 8:20?\",\"options\":[\"135°\",\"130°\",\"120°\",\"230°\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |240 − 110| = 130°.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q7\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 18, 15 and 8 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"41 seconds\",\"180 seconds\",\"720 seconds\",\"360 seconds\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"LCM(18, 15, 8) = 360 seconds.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q8\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"Find the simple interest on Rs 10500 at 6% per annum for 4 years.\",\"options\":[\"Rs 2304\",\"Rs 2369\",\"Rs 2602\",\"Rs 2520\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"SI = P × R × T / 100 = 10500 × 6 × 4 / 100 = Rs 2520.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q9\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 6, 18 and 20 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"360 seconds\",\"90 seconds\",\"180 seconds\",\"44 seconds\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"LCM(6, 18, 20) = 180 seconds.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q10\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"In what ratio must rice at Rs 24/kg be mixed with rice at Rs 72/kg so that the mixture costs Rs 64/kg?\",\"options\":[\"1:5\",\"2:5\",\"24:72\",\"5:1\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Alligation: (cheaper : dearer) = (72 − 64) : (64 − 24) = 1:5.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q11\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"The price of an item is first increased by 10% and then decreased by 20%. What is the net percentage change in its price?\",\"options\":[\"12% decrease\",\"11% decrease\",\"14% decrease\",\"13% decrease\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Net factor = (1 + 10/100)(1 - 20/100) = 22/25, so the change is -12%: a 12% decrease.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q12\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 7:5. After 4 years, the ratio will be 25:19. What is A\'s present age?\",\"options\":[\"15 years\",\"25 years\",\"19 years\",\"21 years\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Let ages be 7x and 5x. (7x+4)/(5x+4) = 25/19 gives x = 3; A = 21.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q13\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"If 4x + 29 = 85, what is x?\",\"options\":[\"17\",\"18\",\"14\",\"10\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"4x = 56, so x = 14.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q14\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"Study the table and answer.\\n\\nYear | Produced (units) | Sold (units)\\n2021 | 300 | 280\\n2022 | 250 | 210\\n2023 | 340 | 280\\n2024 | 240 | 190\\n2025 | 130 | 105\\n\\nIn 2023, what percentage of the units produced was sold? (to 2 decimal places)\",\"options\":[\"17.65%\",\"84.85%\",\"82.35%\",\"80.6%\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"280/340 × 100 = 82.35%.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q15\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 2 be chosen from 6 people?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"30\",\"21\",\"15\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"C(6,2) = 15.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q16\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Asha is 17th from the left and 11th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"28\",\"27\",\"26\",\"29\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 17 + 11 − 1 = 27.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q17\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"What comes next: D, F, H, J, L, ?\",\"options\":[\"N\",\"P\",\"O\",\"M\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 2 places forward.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q18\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Bharat is taller than Kavya. Farhan is taller than Bharat. Jatin is taller than Asha. Kavya is taller than Jatin. Who is the shortest?\",\"options\":[\"Asha\",\"Kavya\",\"Farhan\",\"Bharat\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Chaining the clues: Farhan > Bharat > Kavya > Jatin > Asha. The shortest is Asha.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q19\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Asha is 21st from the left and 20th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"41\",\"39\",\"42\",\"40\"],\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Total = 21 + 20 − 1 = 40.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q20\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Yash walks 12 m towards the East, then turns right and walks 5 m, then turns right and walks 12 m. How far is Yash from the starting point?\",\"options\":[\"4 m\",\"8 m\",\"5 m\",\"1 m\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Net displacement: 0 m east and 5 m south; distance = √(0² + 5²) = 5 m.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q21\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some cars are flowers. All flowers are phones.\\nConclusion: All cars are phones.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q22\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Nikhil is 18th from the left and 17th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"33\",\"35\",\"34\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Total = 18 + 17 − 1 = 34.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q23\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 31, 27, 1000, 125?\",\"options\":[\"27\",\"31\",\"1000\",\"125\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"31 — all others are perfect cubes.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q24\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"In a class of 83 students, 50 like cricket, 44 like football and 23 like both. How many like neither?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"12\",\"35\",\"15\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"83 − (50 + 44 − 23) = 12.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q25\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Asha is 25th from the left and 24th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"48\",\"50\",\"47\",\"49\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Total = 25 + 24 − 1 = 48.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q26\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"What comes next: F, J, N, R, V, ?\",\"options\":[\"B\",\"Z\",\"Y\",\"A\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 4 places forward.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q27\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Lokesh is 24th from the left and 16th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"41\",\"39\",\"38\",\"40\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 24 + 16 − 1 = 39.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q28\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 8, 218, 216, 1000?\",\"options\":[\"218\",\"8\",\"1000\",\"216\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"218 — all others are perfect cubes.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q29\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some teachers are chairs. All chairs are birds.\\nConclusion: All teachers are birds.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q30\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"A man is facing North. He turns right, then turns left, then turns about. Which direction is he facing now?\",\"options\":[\"West\",\"North\",\"East\",\"South\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Right = 90° clockwise, left = 90° anticlockwise, about = 180°. Final direction: South.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q31\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘VIVID’.\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"honest\",\"rough\",\"late\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘vivid’ means bright.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q32\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: The workers went ____ strike yesterday.\",\"options\":[\"at\",\"in\",\"for\",\"on\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: The workers went on strike yesterday.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q33\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Unless you (B) do not work hard, (C) you will not (D) succeed.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘Unless’ is already negative: ‘work hard’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A speech made without preparation\",\"options\":[\"monologue\",\"extempore\",\"sermon\",\"lecture\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A speech made without preparation: extempore.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘hit the nail on the head’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"make a loud noise\",\"hurt someone badly\",\"describe exactly what is causing a problem\",\"work as a carpenter\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘hit the nail on the head’ means: describe exactly what is causing a problem.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ENIGMATIC’.\",\"options\":[\"energetic\",\"emphatic\",\"mysterious\",\"erratic\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘enigmatic’ means mysterious.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is capable ____ handling the pressure.\",\"options\":[\"of\",\"for\",\"at\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is capable of handling the pressure.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Ten kilometres (B) are (C) a long distance (D) to walk.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A distance as one amount: ‘is’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who is easily deceived\",\"options\":[\"cynical\",\"vigilant\",\"sceptical\",\"gullible\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"A person who is easily deceived: gullible.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘cost an arm and a leg’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"need hard work\",\"cause an injury\",\"be cheap\",\"be very expensive\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘cost an arm and a leg’ means: be very expensive.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ALLEVIATE’.\",\"options\":[\"allocate\",\"allude\",\"relieve\",\"alter\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘alleviate’ means relieve.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: No sooner did she arrive ____ the lights went out.\",\"options\":[\"that\",\"than\",\"when\",\"then\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Correct: No sooner did she arrive than the lights went out.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) She (B) has (C) a lot of (D) knowledges.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘Knowledge’ is uncountable: ‘knowledge’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who spends very little\",\"options\":[\"philanthropist\",\"miser\",\"spendthrift\",\"donor\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who spends very little: miser.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘a drop in the ocean’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"a heavy rain\",\"a sea voyage\",\"a big mistake\",\"a very small amount compared to what is needed\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘a drop in the ocean’ means: a very small amount compared to what is needed.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"What does ‘len([1, [2, 3], 4])’ return in Python?\",\"options\":[\"Error\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"The nested list counts as one element.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which device forwards frames using MAC addresses?\",\"options\":[\"Router\",\"Switch\",\"Modem\",\"Hub\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Switches work at layer 2.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"The difference between a process and a thread is that threads\",\"options\":[\"have separate address spaces\",\"always run on different machines\",\"share the memory of their process\",\"cannot run in parallel\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Threads of one process share its address space.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which scheduling algorithm can cause starvation of long jobs?\",\"options\":[\"First Come First Served\",\"Round Robin\",\"Shortest Job First\",\"Multilevel with ageing\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Short jobs keep jumping ahead.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Microservices architecture means\",\"options\":[\"an app built as small independently deployable services\",\"a database type\",\"only front-end code\",\"one large deployable unit\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each service owns one capability.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which traversal uses a stack (explicitly or via recursion)?\",\"options\":[\"Depth-first search\",\"Level-order traversal\",\"Dijkstra with a queue\",\"Breadth-first search\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"DFS goes deep first.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"ACID properties of transactions are\",\"options\":[\"Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\",\"Accuracy, Concurrency, Integrity, Durability\",\"Atomicity, Concurrency, Isolation, Dependency\",\"Availability, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Standard transaction guarantees.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q53\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which testing checks individual functions in isolation?\",\"options\":[\"System testing\",\"Acceptance testing\",\"Load testing\",\"Unit testing\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Smallest testable parts.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q54\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"In MS Excel, which function adds a range of cells?\",\"options\":[\"TOTAL\",\"ADD\",\"SUM\",\"COUNT\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"=SUM(A1:A10).\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q55\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Cloud model where you rent virtual machines and manage the OS yourself:\",\"options\":[\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\",\"FaaS\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Infrastructure as a Service.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q56\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Gmail is an example of\",\"options\":[\"On-premise software\",\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Software delivered over the internet.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q57\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"In C, the size of ‘char’ is\",\"options\":[\"2 bytes\",\"depends on the compiler always 8 bytes\",\"4 bytes\",\"1 byte\"],\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"char is defined as one byte.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q58\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"What is a deadlock?\",\"options\":[\"Memory that cannot be freed\",\"A crashed disk\",\"A process that finishes early\",\"Processes waiting forever for resources held by each other\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Circular wait among processes.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q59\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which normal form removes partial dependencies on a composite key?\",\"options\":[\"2NF\",\"BCNF\",\"3NF\",\"1NF\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"2NF requires full functional dependency on the whole key.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q60\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"ARP is used to find\",\"options\":[\"the IP for a domain\",\"open ports\",\"the MAC address for an IP address\",\"the fastest route\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Address Resolution Protocol.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2026-03-31 10:00:00','2026-03-31 1