t in the rain\",\"very happy\",\"worried about the news\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘under the weather’ means: slightly ill.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: An animal that eats only plants\",\"options\":[\"herbivore\",\"insectivore\",\"omnivore\",\"carnivore\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"An animal that eats only plants: herbivore.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘CORDIAL’.\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"careful\",\"central\",\"cordless\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘cordial’ means warm.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘EMINENT’.\",\"options\":[\"empty\",\"unknown\",\"imminent\",\"distinguished\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘eminent’ means distinguished; its opposite is ‘unknown’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He is senior ____ me by two years.\",\"options\":[\"than\",\"over\",\"from\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He is senior to me by two years.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) I am (B) looking forward (C) to see you (D) soon.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘Looking forward to seeing’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘keep your chin up’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"look at the sky\",\"sit straight\",\"stay positive in difficulty\",\"be proud\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘keep your chin up’ means: stay positive in difficulty.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who does not believe in God\",\"options\":[\"pilgrim\",\"atheist\",\"priest\",\"theist\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who does not believe in God: atheist.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LETHARGIC’.\",\"options\":[\"literal\",\"sluggish\",\"legal\",\"lethal\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘AUGMENT’.\",\"options\":[\"reduce\",\"decorate\",\"increase\",\"observe\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘augment’ means increase; its opposite is ‘reduce’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He apologised ____ being late.\",\"options\":[\"for\",\"about\",\"on\",\"of\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He apologised for being late.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He is (B) an honest (C) and hardworking (D) man.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":4,\"correctOption\":4,\"explanation\":\"The sentence is correct.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2025-07-16 15:00:00','2025-07-16 16:00:00'),('6727c0ab-7d6d-4284-84be-bfa894b6a202','617d3dc4-3697-4d65-9404-ccd3c0b