\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘augment’ means increase; its opposite is ‘reduce’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He apologised ____ being late.\",\"options\":[\"for\",\"about\",\"on\",\"of\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He apologised for being late.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He is (B) an honest (C) and hardworking (D) man.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":4,\"explanation\":\"The sentence is correct.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2026-04-11 00:00:00','2026-04-11 01:00:00'),('7f15f1b4-1d1a-48d6-8c99-7c39e52102f0','617d3dc4-3697-4d65-9404-ccd3c0b8ede3','82264e8d-dbf8-4f31-b553-b20d1ff59cb3','2026-03-22 13:00:00','2026-11-24 19:25:46','2026-03-22 13:34:00',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,29.00,52,'{\"q51\":{\"option\":0},\"q31\":{\"option\":1},\"q30\":{\"option\":0},\"q52\":{\"option\":1},\"q11\":{\"option\":3},\"q33\":{\"option\":1},\"q10\":{\"option\":0},\"q32\":{\"option\":0},\"q13\":{\"option\":3},\"q35\":{\"option\":3},\"q12\":{\"option\":3},\"q34\":{\"option\":1},\"q15\":{\"option\":0},\"q37\":{\"option\":2},\"q14\":{\"option\":2},\"q36\":{\"option\":2},\"q17\":{\"option\":3},\"q16\":{\"option\":0},\"q38\":{\"option\":0},\"q19\":{\"option\":1},\"q18\":{\"option\":1},\"q1\":{\"option\":0},\"q2\":{\"option\":0},\"q3\":{\"option\":2},\"q4\":{\"option\":3},\"q5\":{\"option\":1},\"q6\":{\"option\":0},\"q7\":{\"option\":3},\"q8\":{\"option\":0},\"q9\":{\"option\":1},\"q40\":{\"option\":4},\"q20\":{\"option\":0},\"q42\":{\"option\":3},\"q41\":{\"option\":0},\"q22\":{\"option\":3},\"q44\":{\"option\":2},\"q21\":{\"option\":1},\"q43\":{\"option\":0},\"q24\":{\"option\":3},\"q46\":{\"option\":2},\"q23\":{\"option\":1},\"q45\":{\"option\":3},\"q26\":{\"option\":0},\"q48\":{\"option\":1},\"q47\":{\"option\":2},\"q27\":{\"option\":1},\"q49\":{\"option\":1},\"q29\":{\"option\":0}}',NULL,'{\"attemptId\":\"7f15f1b4-1d1a-48d6-8c99-7c39e52102f0\",\"testId\":\"617d3dc4-3697-4d65-9404-ccd3c0b8ede3\",\"title\":\"Wipro NLTH style · Aptitude\",\"companyTag\":\"Wipro\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:46Z\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:45.769478453Z\",\"timeTakenSeconds\":-1,\"score\":29,\"maxScore\":52,\"percent\":56,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Logical ability\",\"score\":7,\"max\":14,\"correct\":7,\"total\":14},{\"name\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"score\":10,\"max\":16,\"correct\":10,\"total\":16},{\"name\":\"Verbal ability\",\"score\":12,\"max\":22,\"correct\":12,\"total\":22}],\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 27, 8, 28, 729?\",\"options\":[\"27\",\"28\",\"8\",\"729\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"28 — all others are perfect cubes.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 13, 23, 33, 43, 53, ?\",\"options\":[\"63\",\"56\",\"58\",\"60\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rule: add 10 each time. Next term = 63.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"11 : 25 :: 7 : ?\",\"options\":[\"20\",\"18\",\"15\",\"17\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"The rule is n → 2n + 3; for 7 it gives 17.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"If 2 ⊕ 5 = 29; 6 ⊕ 5 = 61, then 9 ⊕ 5 = ?\",\"options\":[\"93\",\"123\",\"103\",\"106\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"a ⊕ b = a² + b²; so 9 ⊕ 5 = 106.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Isha is 12th from the left and 8th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"20\",\"19\",\"21\",\"18\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 12 + 8 − 1 = 19.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some phones are chairs. No chairs is pens.\\nConclusion: Some phones are not pens.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion must hold in every possible case.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q7\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 3, 13, 43, 133, 403, ?\",\"options\":[\"1076\",\"1213\",\"1285\",\"1086\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Rule: multiply by 3 and add 4. Next term = 1213.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q8\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Esha is the father of Yash. Yash is the sister of Kavya. How is Esha related to Kavya?\",\"options\":[\"Father\",\"Grandfather\",\"Brother\",\"Uncle\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Kavya is Yash\'s sibling, so Esha is Kavya\'s father too.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q9\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"If 9 ⊕ 6 = 69; 3 ⊕ 8 = 35, then 9 ⊕ 5 = ?\",\"options\":[\"59\",\"52\",\"67\",\"68\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"a ⊕ b = ab + a + b; so 9 ⊕ 5 = 59.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q10\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Gita is the mother of Chitra. Meera is the son of Chitra. How is Gita related to Meera?\",\"options\":[\"Grandmother\",\"Mother\",\"Sister\",\"Aunt\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Gita is the mother of Meera\'s parent.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q11\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 3, 10, 24, 52, 108, ?\",\"options\":[\"215\",\"218\",\"220\",\"241\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Rule: multiply by 2 and add 4. Next term = 220.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q12\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Bharat is taller than Kavya. Kavya is taller than Rahul. Pooja is taller than Ojas. Rahul is taller than Pooja. Who is the shortest?\",\"options\":[\"Kavya\",\"Bharat\",\"Rahul\",\"Ojas\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Chaining the clues: Bharat > Kavya > Rahul > Pooja > Ojas. The shortest is Ojas.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q13\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 5, 12, 26, 54, 110, ?\",\"options\":[\"225\",\"198\",\"222\",\"227\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Rule: multiply by 2 and add 2. Next term = 222.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q14\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next: H, K, N, Q, T, ?\",\"options\":[\"Y\",\"V\",\"X\",\"W\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 3 places forward.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q15\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A train 300 m long passes a pole in 18 seconds. What is its speed in km/h?\",\"options\":[\"60 km/h\",\"50/3 km/h\",\"66 km/h\",\"56 km/h\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"300/18 m/s × 18/5 = 60 km/h.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q16\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A can finish a work in 40 days and B in 10 days. In how many days will they finish it working together?\",\"options\":[\"8 days\",\"15/2 days\",\"9 days\",\"25 days\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Together per day: 1/40 + 1/10 = 1/8; time = 8 days.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q17\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 5:3. After 8 years, the ratio will be 7:5. What is A\'s present age?\",\"options\":[\"20 years\",\"12 years\",\"28 years\",\"18 years\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Let ages be 5x and 3x. (5x+8)/(3x+8) = 7/5 gives x = 4; A = 20.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q18\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A can finish a work in 24 days and B in 40 days. In how many days will they finish it working together?\",\"options\":[\"32 days\",\"16 days\",\"29/2 days\",\"15 days\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Together per day: 1/24 + 1/40 = 1/15; time = 15 days.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q19\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"In what ratio must rice at Rs 30/kg be mixed with rice at Rs 54/kg so that the mixture costs Rs 35/kg?\",\"options\":[\"30:54\",\"19:5\",\"5:19\",\"20:5\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Alligation: (cheaper : dearer) = (54 − 35) : (35 − 30) = 19:5.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q20\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"Two pipes can fill a tank in 8 hours and 24 hours. How long will they take to fill it together?\",\"options\":[\"6 hours\",\"7 hours\",\"11/2 hours\",\"13/2 hours\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rate = 1/8 + 1/24 = 1/6; time = 6 hours.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q21\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 3 be chosen from 7 people?\",\"options\":[\"35\",\"210\",\"42\",\"70\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"C(7,3) = 35.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q22\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"If today is Wednesday, what day of the week will it be after 294 days?\",\"options\":[\"Thursday\",\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"294 mod 7 = 0; Wednesday + 0 days = Wednesday.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q23\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A starts a business with Rs 9000. After 6 months B joins with Rs 3000. At the end of the year the profit is Rs 1400. What is B\'s share?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 700\",\"Rs 200\",\"Rs 1200\",\"Rs 350\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Ratio = 9000×12 : 3000×6 = 108000:18000; B gets 1400 × 18000/126000 = Rs 200.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q24\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 3 be chosen from 8 people?\",\"options\":[\"112\",\"64\",\"56\",\"336\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"C(8,3) = 56.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q25\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"What is the compound interest on Rs 16000 at 20% per annum for 2 years, compounded annually?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 7090\",\"Rs 6400\",\"Rs 7040\",\"Rs 7020\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"A = 16000(1 + 20/100)^2 = 23040; CI = A − P = Rs 7040.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q26\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"Two pipes can fill a tank in 15 hours and 12 hours. How long will they take to fill it together?\",\"options\":[\"20/3 hours\",\"23/3 hours\",\"43/6 hours\",\"37/6 hours\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rate = 1/15 + 1/12 = 3/20; time = 20/3 hours.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q27\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"Study the table and answer.\\n\\nYear | Produced (units) | Sold (units)\\n2021 | 320 | 245\\n2022 | 280 | 220\\n2023 | 190 | 180\\n2024 | 130 | 85\\n2025 | 120 | 105\\n\\nIn 2024, what percentage of the units produced was sold? (to 2 decimal places)\",\"options\":[\"34.62%\",\"65.38%\",\"67.88%\",\"63.63%\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"85/130 × 100 = 65.38%.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q28\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A boat goes 26 km downstream in 2 hours and 14 km upstream in 2 hours. What is the speed of the boat in still water?\",\"options\":[\"13 km/h\",\"3 km/h\",\"10 km/h\",\"7 km/h\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Downstream 13 km/h, upstream 7 km/h; boat = average = 10 km/h.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q29\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"What is 20% of 400?\",\"options\":[\"80\",\"75\",\"71\",\"87\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"20/100 × 400 = 80.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q30\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A shopkeeper buys an article for Rs 600 and sells it at a profit of 12%. What is the selling price?\",\"options\":[\"672\",\"630\",\"729\",\"715\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"SP = 600 × (100 + 12)/100 = Rs 672.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q31\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LENIENT’.\",\"options\":[\"lean\",\"tolerant\",\"lethal\",\"lengthy\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘lenient’ means tolerant.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q32\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘HAMPER’.\",\"options\":[\"help\",\"handle\",\"hinder\",\"hammer\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘hamper’ means hinder; its opposite is ‘help’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q33\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: You should ____ your doctor before taking this medicine.\",\"options\":[\"consult\",\"insult\",\"result\",\"exult\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: You should consult your doctor before taking this medicine.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) She (B) prefers coffee (C) than (D) tea.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘Prefer … to’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘let the cat out of the bag’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"reveal a secret\",\"free an animal\",\"make a mistake in shopping\",\"go on a trip\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘let the cat out of the bag’ means: reveal a secret.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who has retired from work\",\"options\":[\"trainee\",\"freelancer\",\"pensioner\",\"apprentice\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"A person who has retired from work: pensioner.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘IMMENSE’.\",\"options\":[\"innocent\",\"huge\",\"idle\",\"intense\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘immense’ means huge.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘LETHARGIC’.\",\"options\":[\"energetic\",\"sluggish\",\"lethal\",\"legal\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish; its opposite is ‘energetic’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is ____ honest woman.\",\"options\":[\"the\",\"a\",\"an\",\"no article\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is an honest woman.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He did not (B) knew the answer (C) to the last (D) question.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":4,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"After ‘did not’ use the base form: ‘know’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘under the weather’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"slightly ill\",\"out in the rain\",\"very happy\",\"worried about the news\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘under the weather’ means: slightly ill.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: An animal that eats only plants\",\"options\":[\"herbivore\",\"insectivore\",\"omnivore\",\"carnivore\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"An animal that eats only plants: herbivore.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘CORDIAL’.\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"careful\",\"central\",\"cordless\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘cordial’ means warm.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘EMINENT’.\",\"options\":[\"empty\",\"unknown\",\"imminent\",\"distinguished\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘eminent’ means distinguished; its opposite is ‘unknown’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He is senior ____ me by two years.\",\"options\":[\"than\",\"over\",\"from\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He is senior to me by two years.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) I am (B) looking forward (C) to see you (D) soon.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘Looking forward to seeing’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘keep your chin up’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"look at the sky\",\"sit straight\",\"stay positive in difficulty\",\"be proud\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘keep your chin up’ means: stay positive in difficulty.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who does not believe in God\",\"options\":[\"pilgrim\",\"atheist\",\"priest\",\"theist\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who does not believe in God: atheist.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LETHARGIC’.\",\"options\":[\"literal\",\"sluggish\",\"legal\",\"lethal\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘AUGMENT’.\",\"options\":[\"reduce\",\"decorate\",\"increase\",\"observe\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘augment’ means increase; its opposite is ‘reduce’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He apologised ____ being late.\",\"options\":[\"for\",\"about\",\"on\",\"of\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He apologised for being late.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He is (B) an honest (C) and hardworking (D) man.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":4,\"explanation\":\"The sentence is correct.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2026-03-22 13:00:00','2026-03-22 14:00:00'),('7f264ada-84a3-4f4e-9ecb-65eecfec1285','72213566-2c52-4e3d-9fbd-8e841e9040cc','5f71e5da-65a0-4f0b-a8c2-3483898534cc','2026-03-25 10:00:00','2026-11-24 19:37:43','2026-03-25 10:47:00',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,37.00,60,'{\"q31\":{\"option\":0},\"q30\":{\"option\":3},\"q33\":{\"option\":0},\"q32\":{\"option\":3},\"q35\":{\"option\":2},\"q34\":{\"option\":1},\"q37\":{\"option\":2},\"q39\":{\"option\":2},\"q38\":{\"option\":1},\"q40\":{\"option\":3},\"q42\":{\"option\":1},\"q41\":{\"option\":2},\"q43\":{\"option\":1},\"q46\":{\"option\":1},\"q45\":{\"option\":3},\"q48\":{\"option\":0},\"q47\":{\"option\":2},\"q49\":{\"option\":2},\"q51\":{\"option\":0},\"q50\":{\"option\":3},\"q52\":{\"option\":0},\"q11\":{\"option\":0},\"q10\":{\"option\":0},\"q54\":{\"option\":3},\"q13\":{\"option\":2},\"q57\":{\"option\":3},\"q12\":{\"option\":3},\"q56\":{\"option\":1},\"q15\":{\"option\":0},\"q59\":{\"option\":0},\"q14\":{\"option\":2},\"q58\":{\"option\":2},\"q17\":{\"option\":0},\"q16\":{\"option\":1},\"q19\":{\"option\":2},\"q18\":{\"option\":1},\"q1\":{\"option\":0},\"q2\":{\"option\":3},\"q4\":{\"option\":0},\"q5\":{\"option\":2},\"q6\":{\"option\":1},\"q7\":{\"option\":3},\"q8\":{\"option\":2},\"q9\":{\"option\":3},\"q60\":{\"option\":0},\"q20\":{\"option\":2},\"q22\":{\"option\":3},\"q21\":{\"option\":1},\"q24\":{\"option\":1},\"q23\":{\"option\":1},\"q26\":{\"option\":1},\"q25\":{\"option\":0},\"q28\":{\"option\":0},\"q27\":{\"option\":1},\"q29\":{\"option\":0}}',NULL,'{\"attemptId\":\"7f264ada-84a3-4f4e-9ecb-65eecfec1285\",\"testId\":\"72213566-2c52-4e3d-9fbd-8e841e9040cc\",\"title\":\"HCLTech style · Aptitude + Computer basics\",\"companyTag\":\"HCLTech\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:43Z\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:42.951828397Z\",\"timeTakenSeconds\":-1,\"score\":37,\"maxScore\":60,\"percent\":62,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Quantitative\",\"score\":10,\"max\":15,\"correct\":10,\"total\":15},{\"name\":\"Logical\",\"score\":12,\"max\":15,\"correct\":12,\"total\":15},{\"name\":\"Verbal\",\"score\":9,\"max\":15,\"correct\":9,\"total\":15},{\"name\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"score\":6,\"max\":15,\"correct\":6,\"total\":15}],\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"If 6x + 21 = 99, what is x?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"11\",\"12\",\"13\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"6x = 78, so x = 13.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"A can finish a work in 20 days and B in 40 days. In how many days will they finish it working together?\",\"options\":[\"30 days\",\"77/6 days\",\"43/3 days\",\"40/3 days\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Together per day: 1/20 + 1/40 = 3/40; time = 40/3 days.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"What is the smaller angle between the hour and minute hands of a clock at 2:50?\",\"options\":[\"215°\",\"145°\",\"240°\",\"150°\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |60 − 275| = 145°.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"A train 120 m long passes a pole in 9 seconds. What is its speed in km/h?\",\"options\":[\"48 km/h\",\"40/3 km/h\",\"44 km/h\",\"54 km/h\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"120/9 m/s × 18/5 = 48 km/h.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"A rectangular field is 38 m long and 15 m wide. What is the cost of fencing it at Rs 15 per metre?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 1740\",\"Rs 8550\",\"Rs 1590\",\"Rs 795\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Perimeter = 2(38+15) = 106 m; cost = 106 × 15 = Rs 1590.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"What is the smaller angle between the hour and minute hands of a clock at 8:20?\",\"options\":[\"135°\",\"130°\",\"120°\",\"230°\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |240 − 110| = 130°.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q7\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 18, 15 and 8 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"41 seconds\",\"180 seconds\",\"720 seconds\",\"360 seconds\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"LCM(18, 15, 8) = 360 seconds.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q8\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"Find the simple interest on Rs 10500 at 6% per annum for 4 years.\",\"options\":[\"Rs 2304\",\"Rs 2369\",\"Rs 2602\",\"Rs 2520\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"SI = P × R × T / 100 = 10500 × 6 × 4 / 100 = Rs 2520.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q9\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 6, 18 and 20 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"360 seconds\",\"90 seconds\",\"180 seconds\",\"44 seconds\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"LCM(6, 18, 20) = 180 seconds.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q10\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"In what ratio must rice at Rs 24/kg be mixed with rice at Rs 72/kg so that the mixture costs Rs 64/kg?\",\"options\":[\"1:5\",\"2:5\",\"24:72\",\"5:1\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Alligation: (cheaper : dearer) = (72 − 64) : (64 − 24) = 1:5.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q11\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"The price of an item is first increased by 10% and then decreased by 20%. What is the net percentage change in its price?\",\"options\":[\"12% decrease\",\"11% decrease\",\"14% decrease\",\"13% decrease\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Net factor = (1 + 10/100)(1 - 20/100) = 22/25, so the change is -12%: a 12% decrease.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q12\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 7:5. After 4 years, the ratio will be 25:19. What is A\'s present age?\",\"options\":[\"15 years\",\"25 years\",\"19 years\",\"21 years\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Let ages be 7x and 5x. (7x+4)/(5x+4) = 25/19 gives x = 3; A = 21.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q13\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"If 4x + 29 = 85, what is x?\",\"options\":[\"17\",\"18\",\"14\",\"10\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"4x = 56, so x = 14.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q14\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"Study the table and answer.\\n\\nYear | Produced (units) | Sold (units)\\n2021 | 300 | 280\\n2022 | 250 | 210\\n2023 | 340 | 280\\n2024 | 240 | 190\\n2025 | 130 | 105\\n\\nIn 2023, what percentage of the units produced was sold? (to 2 decimal places)\",\"options\":[\"17.65%\",\"84.85%\",\"82.35%\",\"80.6%\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"280/340 × 100 = 82.35%.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q15\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 2 be chosen from 6 people?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"30\",\"21\",\"15\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"C(6,2) = 15.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q16\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Asha is 17th from the left and 11th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"28\",\"27\",\"26\",\"29\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 17 + 11 − 1 = 27.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q17\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"What comes next: D, F, H, J, L, ?\",\"options\":[\"N\",\"P\",\"O\",\"M\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 2 places forward.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q18\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Bharat is taller than Kavya. Farhan is taller than Bharat. Jatin is taller than Asha. Kavya is taller than Jatin. Who is the shortest?\",\"options\":[\"Asha\",\"Kavya\",\"Farhan\",\"Bharat\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Chaining the clues: Farhan > Bharat > Kavya > Jatin > Asha. The shortest is Asha.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q19\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Asha is 21st from the left and 20th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"41\",\"39\",\"42\",\"40\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Total = 21 + 20 − 1 = 40.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q20\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Yash walks 12 m towards the East, then turns right and walks 5 m, then turns right and walks 12 m. How far is Yash from the starting point?\",\"options\":[\"4 m\",\"8 m\",\"5 m\",\"1 m\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Net displacement: 0 m east and 5 m south; distance = √(0² + 5²) = 5 m.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q21\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some cars are flowers. All flowers are phones.\\nConclusion: All cars are phones.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q22\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Nikhil is 18th from the left and 17th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"33\",\"35\",\"34\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Total = 18 + 17 − 1 = 34.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q23\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 31, 27, 1000, 125?\",\"options\":[\"27\",\"31\",\"1000\",\"125\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"31 — all others are perfect cubes.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q24\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"In a class of 83 students, 50 like cricket, 44 like football and 23 like both. How many like neither?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"12\",\"35\",\"15\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"83 − (50 + 44 − 23) = 12.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q25\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Asha is 25th from the left and 24th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"48\",\"50\",\"47\",\"49\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Total = 25 + 24 − 1 = 48.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q26\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"What comes next: F, J, N, R, V, ?\",\"options\":[\"B\",\"Z\",\"Y\",\"A\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 4 places forward.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q27\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Lokesh is 24th from the left and 16th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"41\",\"39\",\"38\",\"40\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 24 + 16 − 1 = 39.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q28\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 8, 218, 216, 1000?\",\"options\":[\"218\",\"8\",\"1000\",\"216\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"218 — all others are perfect cubes.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q29\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some teachers are chairs. All chairs are birds.\\nConclusion: All teachers are birds.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q30\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical\",\"text\":\"A man is facing North. He turns right, then turns left, then turns about. Which direction is he facing now?\",\"options\":[\"West\",\"North\",\"East\",\"South\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Right = 90° clockwise, left = 90° anticlockwise, about = 180°. Final direction: South.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q31\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘VIVID’.\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"honest\",\"rough\",\"late\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘vivid’ means bright.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q32\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: The workers went ____ strike yesterday.\",\"options\":[\"at\",\"in\",\"for\",\"on\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: The workers went on strike yesterday.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q33\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Unless you (B) do not work hard, (C) you will not (D) succeed.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘Unless’ is already negative: ‘work hard’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A speech made without preparation\",\"options\":[\"monologue\",\"extempore\",\"sermon\",\"lecture\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A speech made without preparation: extempore.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘hit the nail on the head’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"make a loud noise\",\"hurt someone badly\",\"describe exactly what is causing a problem\",\"work as a carpenter\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘hit the nail on the head’ means: describe exactly what is causing a problem.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ENIGMATIC’.\",\"options\":[\"energetic\",\"emphatic\",\"mysterious\",\"erratic\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘enigmatic’ means mysterious.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is capable ____ handling the pressure.\",\"options\":[\"of\",\"for\",\"at\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is capable of handling the pressure.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Ten kilometres (B) are (C) a long distance (D) to walk.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A distance as one amount: ‘is’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who is easily deceived\",\"options\":[\"cynical\",\"vigilant\",\"sceptical\",\"gullible\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"A person who is easily deceived: gullible.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘cost an arm and a leg’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"need hard work\",\"cause an injury\",\"be cheap\",\"be very expensive\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘cost an arm and a leg’ means: be very expensive.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ALLEVIATE’.\",\"options\":[\"allocate\",\"allude\",\"relieve\",\"alter\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘alleviate’ means relieve.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: No sooner did she arrive ____ the lights went out.\",\"options\":[\"that\",\"than\",\"when\",\"then\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Correct: No sooner did she arrive than the lights went out.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) She (B) has (C) a lot of (D) knowledges.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘Knowledge’ is uncountable: ‘knowledge’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who spends very little\",\"options\":[\"philanthropist\",\"miser\",\"spendthrift\",\"donor\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who spends very little: miser.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘a drop in the ocean’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"a heavy rain\",\"a sea voyage\",\"a big mistake\",\"a very small amount compared to what is needed\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘a drop in the ocean’ means: a very small amount compared to what is needed.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"What does ‘len([1, [2, 3], 4])’ return in Python?\",\"options\":[\"Error\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"The nested list counts as one element.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which device forwards frames using MAC addresses?\",\"options\":[\"Router\",\"Switch\",\"Modem\",\"Hub\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Switches work at layer 2.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"The difference between a process and a thread is that threads\",\"options\":[\"have separate address spaces\",\"always run on different machines\",\"share the memory of their process\",\"cannot run in parallel\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Threads of one process share its address space.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which scheduling algorithm can cause starvation of long jobs?\",\"options\":[\"First Come First Served\",\"Round Robin\",\"Shortest Job First\",\"Multilevel with ageing\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Short jobs keep jumping ahead.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Microservices architecture means\",\"options\":[\"an app built as small independently deployable services\",\"a database type\",\"only front-end code\",\"one large deployable unit\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each service owns one capability.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which traversal uses a stack (explicitly or via recursion)?\",\"options\":[\"Depth-first search\",\"Level-order traversal\",\"Dijkstra with a queue\",\"Breadth-first search\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"DFS goes deep first.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"ACID properties of transactions are\",\"options\":[\"Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\",\"Accuracy, Concurrency, Integrity, Durability\",\"Atomicity, Concurrency, Isolation, Dependency\",\"Availability, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Standard transaction guarantees.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q53\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which testing checks individual functions in isolation?\",\"options\":[\"System testing\",\"Acceptance testing\",\"Load testing\",\"Unit testing\"],\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Smallest testable parts.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q54\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"In MS Excel, which function adds a range of cells?\",\"options\":[\"TOTAL\",\"ADD\",\"SUM\",\"COUNT\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"=SUM(A1:A10).\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q55\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Cloud model where you rent virtual machines and manage the OS yourself:\",\"options\":[\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\",\"FaaS\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Infrastructure as a Service.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q56\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Gmail is an example of\",\"options\":[\"On-premise software\",\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Software delivered over the internet.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q57\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"In C, the size of ‘char’ is\",\"options\":[\"2 bytes\",\"depends on the compiler always 8 bytes\",\"4 bytes\",\"1 byte\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"char is defined as one byte.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q58\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"What is a deadlock?\",\"options\":[\"Memory that cannot be freed\",\"A crashed disk\",\"A process that finishes early\",\"Processes waiting forever for resources held by each other\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Circular wait among processes.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q59\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which normal form removes partial dependencies on a composite key?\",\"options\":[\"2NF\",\"BCNF\",\"3NF\",\"1NF\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"2NF requires full functional dependency on the whole key.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q60\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"ARP is used to find\",\"options\":[\"the IP for a domain\",\"open ports\",\"the MAC address for an IP address\",\"the fastest route\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Address Resolution Protocol.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2026-03-25 10:00:00','2026-03-25 11:00:00'),('7fd01174-d6ab-4f90-85ea-cb1d7483c0dd','617d3dc4-3697-4d65-9404-ccd3c0b8ede3','326720cf-4f78-4010-8402-ed7403e4a683','2026-11-23 19:03:31','2026-11-23 19:51:31','2026-11-23 19:03:31',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,13.00,52,'{\"q31\":{\"option\":3},\"q30\":{\"option\":1},\"q52\":{\"option\":4},\"q11\":{\"option\":1},\"q33\":{\"option\":3},\"q10\":{\"option\":2},\"q32\":{\"option\":3},\"q13\":{\"option\":3},\"q35\":{\"option\":1},\"q12\":{\"option\":0},\"q34\":{\"option\":0},\"q15\":{\"option\":2},\"q14\":{\"option\":0},\"q36\":{\"option\":0},\"q17\":{\"option\":0},\"q39\":{\"option\":2},\"q16\":{\"option\":3},\"q38\":{\"option\":2},\"q18\":{\"option\":0},\"q1\":{\"option\":0},\"q2\":{\"option\":2},\"q3\":{\"option\":1},\"q6\":{\"option\":0},\"q7\":{\"option\":2},\"q8\":{\"option\":1},\"q9\":{\"option\":0},\"q40\":{\"option\":2},\"q20\":{\"option\":1},\"q42\":{\"option\":0},\"q41\":{\"option\":3},\"q22\":{\"option\":1},\"q44\":{\"option\":3},\"q21\":{\"option\":0},\"q43\":{\"option\":0},\"q46\":{\"option\":2},\"q45\":{\"option\":1},\"q26\":{\"option\":0},\"q48\":{\"option\":1},\"q25\":{\"option\":3},\"q47\":{\"option\":0},\"q28\":{\"option\":2},\"q49\":{\"option\":1},\"q29\":{\"option\":3}}',NULL,'{\"attemptId\":\"7fd01174-d6ab-4f90-85ea-cb1d7483c0dd\",\"testId\":\"617d3dc4-3697-4d65-9404-ccd3c0b8ede3\",\"title\":\"Wipro NLTH style · Aptitude\",\"companyTag\":\"Wipro\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-23T19:03:31Z\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-11-23T19:03:30.750304189Z\",\"timeTakenSeconds\":-1,\"score\":13,\"maxScore\":52,\"percent\":25,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Logical ability\",\"score\":2,\"max\":14,\"correct\":2,\"total\":14},{\"name\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"score\":4,\"max\":16,\"correct\":4,\"total\":16},{\"name\":\"Verbal ability\",\"score\":7,\"max\":22,\"correct\":7,\"total\":22}],\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 27, 8, 28, 729?\",\"options\":[\"27\",\"28\",\"8\",\"729\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"28 — all others are perfect cubes.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 13, 23, 33, 43, 53, ?\",\"options\":[\"63\",\"56\",\"58\",\"60\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rule: add 10 each time. Next term = 63.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"11 : 25 :: 7 : ?\",\"options\":[\"20\",\"18\",\"15\",\"17\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"The rule is n → 2n + 3; for 7 it gives 17.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"If 2 ⊕ 5 = 29; 6 ⊕ 5 = 61, then 9 ⊕ 5 = ?\",\"options\":[\"93\",\"123\",\"103\",\"106\"],\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"a ⊕ b = a² + b²; so 9 ⊕ 5 = 106.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Isha is 12th from the left and 8th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"20\",\"19\",\"21\",\"18\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 12 + 8 − 1 = 19.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some phones are chairs. No chairs is pens.\\nConclusion: Some phones are not pens.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion must hold in every possible case.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q7\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 3, 13, 43, 133, 403, ?\",\"options\":[\"1076\",\"1213\",\"1285\",\"1086\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Rule: multiply by 3 and add 4. Next term = 1213.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q8\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Esha is the father of Yash. Yash is the sister of Kavya. How is Esha related to Kavya?\",\"options\":[\"Father\",\"Grandfather\",\"Brother\",\"Uncle\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Kavya is Yash\'s sibling, so Esha is Kavya\'s father too.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q9\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"If 9 ⊕ 6 = 69; 3 ⊕ 8 = 35, then 9 ⊕ 5 = ?\",\"options\":[\"59\",\"52\",\"67\",\"68\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"a ⊕ b = ab + a + b; so 9 ⊕ 5 = 59.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q10\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Gita is the mother of Chitra. Meera is the son of Chitra. How is Gita related to Meera?\",\"options\":[\"Grandmother\",\"Mother\",\"Sister\",\"Aunt\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Gita is the mother of Meera\'s parent.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q11\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 3, 10, 24, 52, 108, ?\",\"options\":[\"215\",\"218\",\"220\",\"241\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Rule: multiply by 2 and add 4. Next term = 220.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q12\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"Bharat is taller than Kavya. Kavya is taller than Rahul. Pooja is taller than Ojas. Rahul is taller than Pooja. Who is the shortest?\",\"options\":[\"Kavya\",\"Bharat\",\"Rahul\",\"Ojas\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Chaining the clues: Bharat > Kavya > Rahul > Pooja > Ojas. The shortest is Ojas.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q13\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 5, 12, 26, 54, 110, ?\",\"options\":[\"225\",\"198\",\"222\",\"227\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Rule: multiply by 2 and add 2. Next term = 222.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q14\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Logical ability\",\"text\":\"What comes next: H, K, N, Q, T, ?\",\"options\":[\"Y\",\"V\",\"X\",\"W\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 3 places forward.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q15\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A train 300 m long passes a pole in 18 seconds. What is its speed in km/h?\",\"options\":[\"60 km/h\",\"50/3 km/h\",\"66 km/h\",\"56 km/h\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"300/18 m/s × 18/5 = 60 km/h.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q16\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A can finish a work in 40 days and B in 10 days. In how many days will they finish it working together?\",\"options\":[\"8 days\",\"15/2 days\",\"9 days\",\"25 days\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Together per day: 1/40 + 1/10 = 1/8; time = 8 days.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q17\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 5:3. After 8 years, the ratio will be 7:5. What is A\'s present age?\",\"options\":[\"20 years\",\"12 years\",\"28 years\",\"18 years\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Let ages be 5x and 3x. (5x+8)/(3x+8) = 7/5 gives x = 4; A = 20.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q18\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A can finish a work in 24 days and B in 40 days. In how many days will they finish it working together?\",\"options\":[\"32 days\",\"16 days\",\"29/2 days\",\"15 days\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Together per day: 1/24 + 1/40 = 1/15; time = 15 days.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q19\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"In what ratio must rice at Rs 30/kg be mixed with rice at Rs 54/kg so that the mixture costs Rs 35/kg?\",\"options\":[\"30:54\",\"19:5\",\"5:19\",\"20:5\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Alligation: (cheaper : dearer) = (54 − 35) : (35 − 30) = 19:5.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q20\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"Two pipes can fill a tank in 8 hours and 24 hours. How long will they take to fill it together?\",\"options\":[\"6 hours\",\"7 hours\",\"11/2 hours\",\"13/2 hours\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rate = 1/8 + 1/24 = 1/6; time = 6 hours.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q21\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 3 be chosen from 7 people?\",\"options\":[\"35\",\"210\",\"42\",\"70\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"C(7,3) = 35.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q22\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"If today is Wednesday, what day of the week will it be after 294 days?\",\"options\":[\"Thursday\",\"Monday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Wednesday\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"294 mod 7 = 0; Wednesday + 0 days = Wednesday.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q23\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A starts a business with Rs 9000. After 6 months B joins with Rs 3000. At the end of the year the profit is Rs 1400. What is B\'s share?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 700\",\"Rs 200\",\"Rs 1200\",\"Rs 350\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Ratio = 9000×12 : 3000×6 = 108000:18000; B gets 1400 × 18000/126000 = Rs 200.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q24\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 3 be chosen from 8 people?\",\"options\":[\"112\",\"64\",\"56\",\"336\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"C(8,3) = 56.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q25\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"What is the compound interest on Rs 16000 at 20% per annum for 2 years, compounded annually?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 7090\",\"Rs 6400\",\"Rs 7040\",\"Rs 7020\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"A = 16000(1 + 20/100)^2 = 23040; CI = A − P = Rs 7040.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q26\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"Two pipes can fill a tank in 15 hours and 12 hours. How long will they take to fill it together?\",\"options\":[\"20/3 hours\",\"23/3 hours\",\"43/6 hours\",\"37/6 hours\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rate = 1/15 + 1/12 = 3/20; time = 20/3 hours.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q27\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"Study the table and answer.\\n\\nYear | Produced (units) | Sold (units)\\n2021 | 320 | 245\\n2022 | 280 | 220\\n2023 | 190 | 180\\n2024 | 130 | 85\\n2025 | 120 | 105\\n\\nIn 2024, what percentage of the units produced was sold? (to 2 decimal places)\",\"options\":[\"34.62%\",\"65.38%\",\"67.88%\",\"63.63%\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"85/130 × 100 = 65.38%.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q28\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A boat goes 26 km downstream in 2 hours and 14 km upstream in 2 hours. What is the speed of the boat in still water?\",\"options\":[\"13 km/h\",\"3 km/h\",\"10 km/h\",\"7 km/h\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Downstream 13 km/h, upstream 7 km/h; boat = average = 10 km/h.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q29\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"What is 20% of 400?\",\"options\":[\"80\",\"75\",\"71\",\"87\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"20/100 × 400 = 80.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q30\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Quantitative ability\",\"text\":\"A shopkeeper buys an article for Rs 600 and sells it at a profit of 12%. What is the selling price?\",\"options\":[\"672\",\"630\",\"729\",\"715\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"SP = 600 × (100 + 12)/100 = Rs 672.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q31\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LENIENT’.\",\"options\":[\"lean\",\"tolerant\",\"lethal\",\"lengthy\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘lenient’ means tolerant.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q32\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘HAMPER’.\",\"options\":[\"help\",\"handle\",\"hinder\",\"hammer\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘hamper’ means hinder; its opposite is ‘help’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q33\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: You should ____ your doctor before taking this medicine.\",\"options\":[\"consult\",\"insult\",\"result\",\"exult\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: You should consult your doctor before taking this medicine.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) She (B) prefers coffee (C) than (D) tea.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘Prefer … to’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘let the cat out of the bag’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"reveal a secret\",\"free an animal\",\"make a mistake in shopping\",\"go on a trip\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘let the cat out of the bag’ means: reveal a secret.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who has retired from work\",\"options\":[\"trainee\",\"freelancer\",\"pensioner\",\"apprentice\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"A person who has retired from work: pensioner.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘IMMENSE’.\",\"options\":[\"innocent\",\"huge\",\"idle\",\"intense\"],\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘immense’ means huge.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘LETHARGIC’.\",\"options\":[\"energetic\",\"sluggish\",\"lethal\",\"legal\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish; its opposite is ‘energetic’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is ____ honest woman.\",\"options\":[\"the\",\"a\",\"an\",\"no article\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is an honest woman.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He did not (B) knew the answer (C) to the last (D) question.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"After ‘did not’ use the base form: ‘know’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘under the weather’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"slightly ill\",\"out in the rain\",\"very happy\",\"worried about the news\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘under the weather’ means: slightly ill.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: An animal that eats only plants\",\"options\":[\"herbivore\",\"insectivore\",\"omnivore\",\"carnivore\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"An animal that eats only plants: herbivore.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘CORDIAL’.\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"careful\",\"central\",\"cordless\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘cordial’ means warm.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘EMINENT’.\",\"options\":[\"empty\",\"unknown\",\"imminent\",\"distinguished\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘eminent’ means distinguished; its opposite is ‘unknown’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He is senior ____ me by two years.\",\"options\":[\"than\",\"over\",\"from\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He is senior to me by two years.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) I am (B) looking forward (C) to see you (D) soon.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘Looking forward to seeing’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘keep your chin up’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"look at the sky\",\"sit straight\",\"stay positive in difficulty\",\"be proud\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘keep your chin up’ means: stay positive in difficulty.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who does not believe in God\",\"options\":[\"pilgrim\",\"atheist\",\"priest\",\"theist\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who does not believe in God: atheist.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LETHARGIC’.\",\"options\":[\"literal\",\"sluggish\",\"legal\",\"lethal\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘AUGMENT’.\",\"options\":[\"reduce\",\"decorate\",\"increase\",\"observe\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘augment’ means increase; its opposite is ‘reduce’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: He apologised ____ being late.\",\"options\":[\"for\",\"about\",\"on\",\"of\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: He apologised for being late.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He is (B) an honest (C) and hardworking (D) man.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":4,\"correctOption\":4,\"explanation\":\"The sentence is correct.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\