you (B) do not work hard, (C) you will not (D) succeed.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘Unless’ is already negative: ‘work hard’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A speech made without preparation\",\"options\":[\"monologue\",\"extempore\",\"sermon\",\"lecture\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A speech made without preparation: extempore.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘hit the nail on the head’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"make a loud noise\",\"hurt someone badly\",\"describe exactly what is causing a problem\",\"work as a carpenter\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘hit the nail on the head’ means: describe exactly what is causing a problem.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ENIGMATIC’.\",\"options\":[\"energetic\",\"emphatic\",\"mysterious\",\"erratic\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘enigmatic’ means mysterious.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is capable ____ handling the pressure.\",\"options\":[\"of\",\"for\",\"at\",\"to\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is capable of handling the pressure.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Ten kilometres (B) are (C) a long distance (D) to walk.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A distance as one amount: ‘is’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who is easily deceived\",\"options\":[\"cynical\",\"vigilant\",\"sceptical\",\"gullible\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"A person who is easily deceived: gullible.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘cost an arm and a leg’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"need hard work\",\"cause an injury\",\"be cheap\",\"be very expensive\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘cost an arm and a leg’ means: be very expensive.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ALLEVIATE’.\",\"options\":[\"allocate\",\"allude\",\"relieve\",\"alter\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘alleviate’ means relieve.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: No sooner did she arrive ____ the lights went out.\",\"options\":[\"that\",\"than\",\"when\",\"then\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Correct: No sooner did she arrive than the lights went out.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) She (B) has (C) a lot of (D) knowledges.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘Knowledge’ is uncountable: ‘knowledge’.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who spends very little\",\"options\":[\"philanthropist\",\"miser\",\"spendthrift\",\"donor\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who spends very little: miser.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘a drop in the ocean’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"a heavy rain\",\"a sea voyage\",\"a big mistake\",\"a very small amount compared to what is needed\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘a drop in the ocean’ means: a very small amount compared to what is needed.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"What does ‘len([1, [2, 3], 4])’ return in Python?\",\"options\":[\"Error\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"The nested list counts as one element.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which device forwards frames using MAC addresses?\",\"options\":[\"Router\",\"Switch\",\"Modem\",\"Hub\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Switches work at layer 2.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"The difference between a process and a thread is that threads\",\"options\":[\"have separate address spaces\",\"always run on different machines\",\"share the memory of their process\",\"cannot run in parallel\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Threads of one process share its address space.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which scheduling algorithm can cause starvation of long jobs?\",\"options\":[\"First Come First Served\",\"Round Robin\",\"Shortest Job First\",\"Multilevel with ageing\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Short jobs keep jumping ahead.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Microservices architecture means\",\"options\":[\"an app built as small independently deployable services\",\"a database type\",\"only front-end code\",\"one large deployable unit\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each service owns one capability.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which traversal uses a stack (explicitly or via recursion)?\",\"options\":[\"Depth-first search\",\"Level-order traversal\",\"Dijkstra with a queue\",\"Breadth-first search\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"DFS goes deep first.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"ACID properties of transactions are\",\"options\":[\"Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\",\"Accuracy, Concurrency, Integrity, Durability\",\"Atomicity, Concurrency, Isolation, Dependency\",\"Availability, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\"],\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"Standard transaction guarantees.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q53\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which testing checks individual functions in isolation?\",\"options\":[\"System testing\",\"Acceptance testing\",\"Load testing\",\"Unit testing\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Smallest testable parts.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q54\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"In MS Excel, which function adds a range of cells?\",\"options\":[\"TOTAL\",\"ADD\",\"SUM\",\"COUNT\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"=SUM(A1:A10).\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q55\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Cloud model where you rent virtual machines and manage the OS yourself:\",\"options\":[\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\",\"FaaS\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Infrastructure as a Service.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q56\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Gmail is an example of\",\"options\":[\"On-premise software\",\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"Software delivered over the internet.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q57\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"In C, the size of ‘char’ is\",\"options\":[\"2 bytes\",\"depends on the compiler always 8 bytes\",\"4 bytes\",\"1 byte\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"char is defined as one byte.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q58\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"What is a deadlock?\",\"options\":[\"Memory that cannot be freed\",\"A crashed disk\",\"A process that finishes early\",\"Processes waiting forever for resources held by each other\"],\"yourOption\":3,\"correctOption\":3,\"explanation\":\"Circular wait among processes.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q59\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"Which normal form removes partial dependencies on a composite key?\",\"options\":[\"2NF\",\"BCNF\",\"3NF\",\"1NF\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"2NF requires full functional dependency on the whole key.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q60\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"text\":\"ARP is used to find\",\"options\":[\"the IP for a domain\",\"open ports\",\"the MAC address for an IP address\",\"the fastest route\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Address Resolution Protocol.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2025-06-06 09:00:00','2025-06-06 10:00:00'),('db27995a-e237-4052-9439-aa969c227595','260c32f9-7de0-4be6-b091-dcd32b1de502','38873e70-9ee4-44a2-b64d-6220451cc321','2025-06-20 22:00:00','2026-11-24 19:07:24','2025-06-20 22:25:00',NULL,NULL,0,0,NULL,4.00,5,'{\"q1\":{\"option\":0},\"q2\":{\"option\":2},\"q3\":{\"option\":1},\"q4\":{\"option\":1},\"q5\":{\"option\":1}}',NULL,'{\"attemptId\":\"db27995a-e237-4052-9439-aa969c227595\",\"testId\":\"260c32f9-7de0-4be6-b091-dcd32b1de502\",\"title\":\"TCS NQT Pattern - Practice Set\",\"companyTag\":\"TCS\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:24Z\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-11-24T18:37:23.730638406Z\",\"timeTakenSeconds\":-1,\"score\":4,\"maxScore\":5,\"percent\":80,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Numerical Ability\",\"score\":2,\"max\":3,\"correct\":2,\"total\":3},{\"name\":\"Verbal Ability\",\"score\":2,\"max\":2,\"correct\":2,\"total\":2}],\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Numerical Ability\",\"text\":\"A shopkeeper sells an item at 20% profit. If the cost price is Rs 500, what is the selling price?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 550\",\"Rs 600\",\"Rs 620\",\"Rs 650\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":1,\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Numerical Ability\",\"text\":\"The average of 5 numbers is 24. If one number is removed the average becomes 22. Which number was removed?\",\"options\":[\"28\",\"30\",\"32\",\"34\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":2,\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Numerical Ability\",\"text\":\"Pipe A fills a tank in 6 hours and pipe B in 3 hours. Together they fill it in:\",\"options\":[\"1.5 h\",\"2 h\",\"2.5 h\",\"4.5 h\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal Ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to \'METICULOUS\'.\",\"options\":[\"Careless\",\"Careful\",\"Quick\",\"Rough\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal Ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She has been working here ____ 2022.\",\"options\":[\"for\",\"since\",\"from\",\"by\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1}],\"released\":true,\"answersShown\":true,\"pendingReview\":false}','2