"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘lethargic’ means sluggish; its opposite is ‘energetic’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is ____ honest woman.\",\"options\":[\"the\",\"a\",\"an\",\"no article\"],\"correctOption\":2,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is an honest woman.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) He did not (B) knew the answer (C) to the last (D) question.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"yourOption\":1,\"correctOption\":1,\"explanation\":\"After ‘did not’ use the base form: ‘know’.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘under the weather’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"slightly ill\",\"out in the rain\",\"very happy\",\"worried about the news\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘under the weather’ means: slightly ill.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"One word for: An animal that eats only plants\",\"options\":[\"herbivore\",\"insectivore\",\"omnivore\",\"carnivore\"],\"yourOption\":2,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"An animal that eats only plants: herbivore.\",\"marksAwarded\":0,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘CORDIAL’.\",\"options\":[\"warm\",\"careful\",\"central\",\"cordless\"],\"yourOption\":0,\"correctOption\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘cordial’ means warm.\",\"marksAwarded\":1,\"marks\":1},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"section\":\"Verbal ability\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘EMINENT’.\",\"options\":[\"empty\",\"unknown\",\"imminent\",\"distinguished\"],\"