\n..........#.........................#...#..#....................#.....#..#.........#..#..#..###............\\n......##........##........#...................#......#......#..#...............#.....#.....#.........#.....\\n..#......#.......#...#.#.......#.........#....................................#....#.......................\\n................#...#..................###....#.#.......................#...............#.......#........#.\\n.#...#..........#.........#...............#...............#.#.......#................#.....................\\n........##...........#.#.............#....................#......................##......#.##..............\\n.............##.....#........#..###...........##..........#..#.......#..........#.#.#...#.....#............\\n...#..#.......##...........#..#.....#....#.#.......#............#........#....#......#...........#.....#.#.\\n...........#.....#..#.#.#......#.......#............#...............#.........................#....#.##....\\n.#............#..#..#....#................#.........#.......#.............#................................\\n.#..#...#.........#..#..........#....#.........#.#......................#.......#......#............#......\\n....#.#......................................#.......#..................#....#...#...............##........\\n.....#.#..........#........#....#......##.#..#..............#......#...............##.........#........#...\\n......#..#.#..#...................#....#..........#...........#..............#.#...#...#............##.....\\n\",\"output\":\"651672555\"},{\"input\":\"3 159\\n..............#..........#.....#........#....#.#.....#..#..............#....##..............................##.....#...............#.#........#............#...\\n..#...#..........#.#.......#......##....#.....#........#....#.............#...........##.........#.......#...........#......#....#...##...#................#...\\n.....#..........#.........#.....................#.........................#.....#...............#.#...........................#.....................#.........#\\n\",\"output\":\"0\"}]}]}]}',1,'PRACTICE',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,1,NULL,'5f867bde-403b-454f-b2f0-6e569995f4f0','2026-11-23 19:03:08','2026-11-23 19:03:08'),('138871f9-5dac-4613-a42d-15ac736ed77b',NULL,'LTIMindtree style · Aptitude + Coding','Aptitude and verbal followed by coding. 45 MCQs + 2 coding problems in 100 minutes. Original practice questions modelled on the publicly reported test pattern. Not an official or past paper.','LTIMindtree','MEDIUM',9,100,47,2,65,'{\"title\":\"LTIMindtree style · Aptitude + Coding\",\"description\":\"Aptitude and verbal followed by coding. 45 MCQs + 2 coding problems in 100 minutes. Original practice questions modelled on the publicly reported test pattern. Not an official or past paper.\",\"companyTag\":\"LTIMindtree\",\"level\":\"MEDIUM\",\"order\":9,\"durationMinutes\":100,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Quantitative\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What is the unit digit of 13^70?\",\"options\":[\"7\",\"1\",\"3\",\"9\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Unit digits of powers of 3 repeat every 4; 70 mod 4 = 2, giving 9.\"},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"A sum of money amounts to Rs 18700 in 2 years at 5% per annum simple interest. What is the sum?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 17500\",\"Rs 16500\",\"Rs 17250\",\"Rs 17000\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Amount = P(1 + 5×2/100) = P × 11/10, so P = 18700 / 11/10 = Rs 17000.\"},{\"id\":\"q3\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"If today is Sunday, what day of the week will it be after 194 days?\",\"options\":[\"Tuesday\",\"Friday\",\"Wednesday\",\"Monday\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"194 mod 7 = 5; Sunday + 5 days = Friday.\"},{\"id\":\"q4\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 12, 24 and 20 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"120 seconds\",\"60 seconds\",\"240 seconds\",\"56 seconds\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"LCM(12, 24, 20) = 120 seconds.\"},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 4:3. After 5 years, the ratio will be 33:26. What is A\'s present age?\",\"options\":[\"28 years\",\"26 years\",\"33 years\",\"21 years\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Let ages be 4x and 3x. (4x+5)/(3x+5) = 33/26 gives x = 7; A = 28.\"},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In how many different ways can the letters of the word LETTER be arranged?\",\"options\":[\"90\",\"180\",\"360\",\"720\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"6! divided by the factorials of repeated letters (E:2, T:2) = 180.\"},{\"id\":\"q7\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Pipes A and B can fill a tank in 12 and 30 hours. Pipe C can empty it in 30 hours. If all three are opened together, how long will the tank take to fill?\",\"options\":[\"12 hours\",\"23/2 hours\",\"13 hours\",\"25/2 hours\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Net rate = 1/12 + 1/30 − 1/30 = 1/12 tank/hour, so 12 hours.\"},{\"id\":\"q8\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"If today is Sunday, what day of the week will it be after 140 days?\",\"options\":[\"Sunday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Monday\",\"Wednesday\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"140 mod 7 = 0; Sunday + 0 days = Sunday.\"},{\"id\":\"q9\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"If today is Thursday, what day of the week will it be after 193 days?\",\"options\":[\"Wednesday\",\"Thursday\",\"Tuesday\",\"Monday\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"193 mod 7 = 4; Thursday + 4 days = Monday.\"},{\"id\":\"q10\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What are the roots of x² - 15x + 56 = 0?\",\"options\":[\"-8 and -7\",\"8 and 9\",\"7 and 8\",\"-8 and 7\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Sum of roots = 15, product = 56: the roots are 7 and 8.\"},{\"id\":\"q11\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In how many different ways can the letters of the word APPLE be arranged?\",\"options\":[\"65\",\"30\",\"60\",\"120\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"5! divided by the factorials of repeated letters (P:2) = 60.\"},{\"id\":\"q12\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"A starts a business with Rs 7000. After 3 months B joins with Rs 10000. At the end of the year the profit is Rs 14500. What is B\'s share?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 8000\",\"Rs 7000\",\"Rs 145000/17\",\"Rs 7500\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Ratio = 7000×12 : 10000×9 = 84000:90000; B gets 14500 × 90000/174000 = Rs 7500.\"},{\"id\":\"q13\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"A bag has 4 red, 5 blue and 6 green balls. Two balls are drawn at random. What is the probability that both are red?\",\"options\":[\"4/15\",\"16/225\",\"2/35\",\"1/15\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"C(4,2)/C(15,2) = 6/105 = 2/35.\"},{\"id\":\"q14\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"A can do a job in 20 days and B in 40 days. They work together for 2 days, then B leaves. In how many more days will A finish the job?\",\"options\":[\"33/2 days\",\"17 days\",\"34 days\",\"18 days\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"In 2 days they do 3/20 of the work; 17/20 is left, which A does in 17/20 × 20 = 17 days.\"},{\"id\":\"q15\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In what ratio must rice at Rs 20/kg be mixed with rice at Rs 72/kg so that the mixture costs Rs 49/kg?\",\"options\":[\"20:72\",\"23:29\",\"29:23\",\"24:29\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Alligation: (cheaper : dearer) = (72 − 49) : (49 − 20) = 23:29.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Logical\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q16\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 64, 256, 16, 19?\",\"options\":[\"16\",\"256\",\"64\",\"19\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"19 — all others are perfect squares.\"},{\"id\":\"q17\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In a row of 21 students, Isha is 13th from the left. Kavya is 8 places to the right of Isha. What is Kavya\'s position from the right end?\",\"options\":[\"2\",\"1\",\"0\",\"21\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Kavya is 21st from the left, so 21 − 21 + 1 = 1st from the right.\"},{\"id\":\"q18\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In a survey, 24 people read newspaper A, 48 read B, 11 read both and 15 read neither. How many people read only one newspaper?\",\"options\":[\"61\",\"35\",\"13\",\"50\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Only A = 13, only B = 37; total = 50.\"},{\"id\":\"q19\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"12 : 27 :: 11 : ?\",\"options\":[\"25\",\"24\",\"23\",\"26\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"The rule is n → 2n + 3; for 11 it gives 25.\"},{\"id\":\"q20\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In a row of 33 students, Uma is 16th from the left. Ojas is 8 places to the right of Uma. What is Ojas\'s position from the right end?\",\"options\":[\"9\",\"10\",\"11\",\"24\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Ojas is 24th from the left, so 33 − 24 + 1 = 10th from the right.\"},{\"id\":\"q21\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"If 8 ⊕ 6 = 62; 4 ⊕ 7 = 39, then 9 ⊕ 8 = ?\",\"options\":[\"76\",\"89\",\"79\",\"101\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"a ⊕ b = ab + a + b; so 9 ⊕ 8 = 89.\"},{\"id\":\"q22\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Statements: All pens are rivers. All rivers are flowers.\\nConclusion: All flowers are pens.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\"},{\"id\":\"q23\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"If 3 ⊕ 9 = 90; 4 ⊕ 9 = 97, then 4 ⊕ 6 = ?\",\"options\":[\"45\",\"52\",\"53\",\"47\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"a ⊕ b = a² + b²; so 4 ⊕ 6 = 52.\"},{\"id\":\"q24\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Introducing a woman, Kavya says, \\\"She is the wife of the only son of my father.\\\" How is the woman related to Kavya?\",\"options\":[\"Sister-in-law\",\"Sister\",\"Mother\",\"Wife\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"The only son of Kavya\'s father is Kavya, so she is Kavya\'s wife.\"},{\"id\":\"q25\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In a certain code, PENCIL is written as ODMBHK. How is GARDEN written in that code?\",\"options\":[\"HBSEFO\",\"GARDEN\",\"FZQCDM\",\"EYPBCL\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Each letter is shifted -1 place in the alphabet.\"},{\"id\":\"q26\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 37, 61, 17, 87?\",\"options\":[\"61\",\"87\",\"37\",\"17\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"87 — all others are prime.\"},{\"id\":\"q27\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 23, 61, 57, 31?\",\"options\":[\"31\",\"57\",\"61\",\"23\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"57 — all others are prime.\"},{\"id\":\"q28\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Meera is taller than Pooja. Nikhil is taller than Gita. Pooja is taller than Asha. Asha is taller than Nikhil. Who is the second tallest?\",\"options\":[\"Asha\",\"Pooja\",\"Meera\",\"Nikhil\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Chaining the clues: Meera > Pooja > Asha > Nikhil > Gita. The second tallest is Pooja.\"},{\"id\":\"q29\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What comes next in the series: 18, 27, 38, 51, 66, ?\",\"options\":[\"83\",\"91\",\"90\",\"81\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Rule: squares of 4, 5, ... plus 2. Next term = 83.\"},{\"id\":\"q30\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 67, 361, 64, 121?\",\"options\":[\"64\",\"121\",\"67\",\"361\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"67 — all others are perfect squares.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Verbal\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q31\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Read the passage and answer.\\n\\nPublic libraries are changing. Besides books, many now offer free internet, study spaces and workshops on coding or job skills. For students who lack a quiet place at home, the library becomes a second classroom. Libraries that adapted in this way have seen visitor numbers rise even as reading habits shift online.\\n\\nWhat happened to libraries that adapted?\",\"options\":[\"Visitor numbers rose\",\"They became private\",\"They closed\",\"They stopped lending books\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"The passage supports: Visitor numbers rose.\"},{\"id\":\"q32\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Each of the boys (B) have brought (C) his own (D) lunch today.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘Each’ is singular: ‘has brought’.\"},{\"id\":\"q33\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Arrange the sentences in the correct order:\\nP: She reached the office before nine.\\nQ: The alarm rang at six.\\nR: After a shower she had breakfast.\\nS: Sneha got up and went for a run.\",\"options\":[\"RSQP\",\"QPRS\",\"SRQP\",\"QSRP\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct order: The alarm rang at six. Sneha got up and went for a run. After a shower she had breakfast. She reached the office before nine.\"},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘INEVITABLE’.\",\"options\":[\"infinite\",\"unavoidable\",\"inedible\",\"invisible\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘inevitable’ means unavoidable.\"},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘TRIVIAL’.\",\"options\":[\"tribal\",\"significant\",\"minor\",\"typical\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘trivial’ means minor; its opposite is ‘significant’.\"},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Read the passage and answer.\\n\\nTeamwork is often judged in interviews through group discussions. Candidates who speak the most do not always do best. Evaluators look for people who listen, build on others\' points, bring the group back to the topic and help reach a conclusion. Interrupting others or repeating the same point usually counts against a candidate.\\n\\nWhat usually counts against a candidate?\",\"options\":[\"Helping reach a conclusion\",\"Interrupting others\",\"Bringing the group back to the topic\",\"Listening carefully\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"The passage supports: Interrupting others.\"},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) The police (B) has arrested (C) the two (D) suspects.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘Police’ takes a plural verb: ‘have arrested’.\"},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Arrange the sentences in the correct order:\\nP: Two days later she received the offer letter.\\nQ: The interview went better than she expected.\\nR: She was called for an interview the next week.\\nS: Meera applied for an internship.\",\"options\":[\"QSPR\",\"QRPS\",\"RSQP\",\"SRQP\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct order: Meera applied for an internship. She was called for an interview the next week. The interview went better than she expected. Two days later she received the offer letter.\"},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ELOQUENT’.\",\"options\":[\"elegant\",\"expressive\",\"elastic\",\"eligible\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘eloquent’ means expressive.\"},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘NOVICE’.\",\"options\":[\"nurse\",\"expert\",\"novel\",\"beginner\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘novice’ means beginner; its opposite is ‘expert’.\"},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Read the passage and answer.\\n\\nElectric vehicles are becoming more common in Indian cities. They produce no exhaust and are cheaper to run than petrol vehicles. Their main drawbacks are a higher purchase price and a shortage of charging stations. As battery prices fall and more chargers are installed, experts expect electric two-wheelers and buses to spread fastest.\\n\\nA drawback mentioned is\",\"options\":[\"lack of buyers in villages\",\"high exhaust\",\"a shortage of charging stations\",\"loud engines\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"The passage supports: a shortage of charging stations.\"},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) One of my friend (B) is going (C) to Canada (D) next week.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘One of my friends’.\"},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Arrange the sentences in the correct order:\\nP: A seed falls on moist soil.\\nQ: It absorbs water and swells.\\nR: Soon a shoot pushes up towards the light.\\nS: A tiny root grows downwards.\",\"options\":[\"RSPQ\",\"PRSQ\",\"PQSR\",\"SQPR\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Correct order: A seed falls on moist soil. It absorbs water and swells. A tiny root grows downwards. Soon a shoot pushes up towards the light.\"},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘LUCID’.\",\"options\":[\"heavy\",\"lucky\",\"warm\",\"clear\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘lucid’ means clear.\"},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘INEVITABLE’.\",\"options\":[\"avoidable\",\"inedible\",\"unavoidable\",\"invisible\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘inevitable’ means unavoidable; its opposite is ‘avoidable’.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Coding\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"CODING\",\"title\":\"Count primes\",\"text\":\"Print how many prime numbers are less than or equal to N.\\n\\nInput: one integer N (1 ≤ N ≤ 10^6).\\nOutput: the count of primes ≤ N.\",\"marks\":10,\"explanation\":\"Reference approach: see the standard technique for ‘Count primes’.\",\"starterCode\":{\"python\":\"import sys\\n\\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\\n# write your code here\\n\",\"java\":\"import java.util.*;\\nimport java.io.*;\\n\\npublic class Main {\\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\\n        // write your code here\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"cpp\":\"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\n