r\":0,\"explanation\":\"120/9 m/s × 18/5 = 48 km/h.\"},{\"id\":\"q5\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"A rectangular field is 38 m long and 15 m wide. What is the cost of fencing it at Rs 15 per metre?\",\"options\":[\"Rs 1740\",\"Rs 8550\",\"Rs 1590\",\"Rs 795\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Perimeter = 2(38+15) = 106 m; cost = 106 × 15 = Rs 1590.\"},{\"id\":\"q6\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What is the smaller angle between the hour and minute hands of a clock at 8:20?\",\"options\":[\"135°\",\"130°\",\"120°\",\"230°\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |240 − 110| = 130°.\"},{\"id\":\"q7\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 18, 15 and 8 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"41 seconds\",\"180 seconds\",\"720 seconds\",\"360 seconds\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"LCM(18, 15, 8) = 360 seconds.\"},{\"id\":\"q8\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Find the simple interest on Rs 10500 at 6% per annum for 4 years.\",\"options\":[\"Rs 2304\",\"Rs 2369\",\"Rs 2602\",\"Rs 2520\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"SI = P × R × T / 100 = 10500 × 6 × 4 / 100 = Rs 2520.\"},{\"id\":\"q9\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"3 bells ring at intervals of 6, 18 and 20 seconds. If they ring together now, after how many seconds will they next ring together?\",\"options\":[\"360 seconds\",\"90 seconds\",\"180 seconds\",\"44 seconds\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"LCM(6, 18, 20) = 180 seconds.\"},{\"id\":\"q10\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In what ratio must rice at Rs 24/kg be mixed with rice at Rs 72/kg so that the mixture costs Rs 64/kg?\",\"options\":[\"1:5\",\"2:5\",\"24:72\",\"5:1\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Alligation: (cheaper : dearer) = (72 − 64) : (64 − 24) = 1:5.\"},{\"id\":\"q11\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"The price of an item is first increased by 10% and then decreased by 20%. What is the net percentage change in its price?\",\"options\":[\"12% decrease\",\"11% decrease\",\"14% decrease\",\"13% decrease\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Net factor = (1 + 10/100)(1 - 20/100) = 22/25, so the change is -12%: a 12% decrease.\"},{\"id\":\"q12\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 7:5. After 4 years, the ratio will be 25:19. What is A\'s present age?\",\"options\":[\"15 years\",\"25 years\",\"19 years\",\"21 years\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Let ages be 7x and 5x. (7x+4)/(5x+4) = 25/19 gives x = 3; A = 21.\"},{\"id\":\"q13\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"If 4x + 29 = 85, what is x?\",\"options\":[\"17\",\"18\",\"14\",\"10\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"4x = 56, so x = 14.\"},{\"id\":\"q14\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Study the table and answer.\\n\\nYear | Produced (units) | Sold (units)\\n2021 | 300 | 280\\n2022 | 250 | 210\\n2023 | 340 | 280\\n2024 | 240 | 190\\n2025 | 130 | 105\\n\\nIn 2023, what percentage of the units produced was sold? (to 2 decimal places)\",\"options\":[\"17.65%\",\"84.85%\",\"82.35%\",\"80.6%\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"280/340 × 100 = 82.35%.\"},{\"id\":\"q15\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In how many ways can a committee of 2 be chosen from 6 people?\",\"options\":[\"12\",\"30\",\"21\",\"15\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"C(6,2) = 15.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Logical\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q16\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Asha is 17th from the left and 11th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"28\",\"27\",\"26\",\"29\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 17 + 11 − 1 = 27.\"},{\"id\":\"q17\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What comes next: D, F, H, J, L, ?\",\"options\":[\"N\",\"P\",\"O\",\"M\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 2 places forward.\"},{\"id\":\"q18\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Bharat is taller than Kavya. Farhan is taller than Bharat. Jatin is taller than Asha. Kavya is taller than Jatin. Who is the shortest?\",\"options\":[\"Asha\",\"Kavya\",\"Farhan\",\"Bharat\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Chaining the clues: Farhan > Bharat > Kavya > Jatin > Asha. The shortest is Asha.\"},{\"id\":\"q19\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Asha is 21st from the left and 20th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"41\",\"39\",\"42\",\"40\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Total = 21 + 20 − 1 = 40.\"},{\"id\":\"q20\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Yash walks 12 m towards the East, then turns right and walks 5 m, then turns right and walks 12 m. How far is Yash from the starting point?\",\"options\":[\"4 m\",\"8 m\",\"5 m\",\"1 m\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Net displacement: 0 m east and 5 m south; distance = √(0² + 5²) = 5 m.\"},{\"id\":\"q21\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some cars are flowers. All flowers are phones.\\nConclusion: All cars are phones.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\"},{\"id\":\"q22\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Nikhil is 18th from the left and 17th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"36\",\"33\",\"35\",\"34\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Total = 18 + 17 − 1 = 34.\"},{\"id\":\"q23\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 31, 27, 1000, 125?\",\"options\":[\"27\",\"31\",\"1000\",\"125\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"31 — all others are perfect cubes.\"},{\"id\":\"q24\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In a class of 83 students, 50 like cricket, 44 like football and 23 like both. How many like neither?\",\"options\":[\"14\",\"12\",\"35\",\"15\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"83 − (50 + 44 − 23) = 12.\"},{\"id\":\"q25\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Asha is 25th from the left and 24th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"48\",\"50\",\"47\",\"49\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Total = 25 + 24 − 1 = 48.\"},{\"id\":\"q26\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What comes next: F, J, N, R, V, ?\",\"options\":[\"B\",\"Z\",\"Y\",\"A\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Each letter moves 4 places forward.\"},{\"id\":\"q27\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Lokesh is 24th from the left and 16th from the right in a row. How many people are in the row?\",\"options\":[\"41\",\"39\",\"38\",\"40\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Total = 24 + 16 − 1 = 39.\"},{\"id\":\"q28\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which number is the odd one out: 8, 218, 216, 1000?\",\"options\":[\"218\",\"8\",\"1000\",\"216\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"218 — all others are perfect cubes.\"},{\"id\":\"q29\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Statements: Some teachers are chairs. All chairs are birds.\\nConclusion: All teachers are birds.\\nDoes the conclusion follow?\",\"options\":[\"The conclusion definitely follows\",\"The conclusion does not follow\",\"The data is contradictory\",\"The conclusion is partly true\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Draw the Venn diagram for the statements: the conclusion fails in at least one possible case.\"},{\"id\":\"q30\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"A man is facing North. He turns right, then turns left, then turns about. Which direction is he facing now?\",\"options\":[\"West\",\"North\",\"East\",\"South\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Right = 90° clockwise, left = 90° anticlockwise, about = 180°. Final direction: South.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Verbal\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q31\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘VIVID’.\",\"options\":[\"bright\",\"honest\",\"rough\",\"late\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"‘vivid’ means bright.\"},{\"id\":\"q32\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: The workers went ____ strike yesterday.\",\"options\":[\"at\",\"in\",\"for\",\"on\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Correct: The workers went on strike yesterday.\"},{\"id\":\"q33\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Unless you (B) do not work hard, (C) you will not (D) succeed.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"‘Unless’ is already negative: ‘work hard’.\"},{\"id\":\"q34\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"One word for: A speech made without preparation\",\"options\":[\"monologue\",\"extempore\",\"sermon\",\"lecture\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"A speech made without preparation: extempore.\"},{\"id\":\"q35\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘hit the nail on the head’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"make a loud noise\",\"hurt someone badly\",\"describe exactly what is causing a problem\",\"work as a carpenter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘hit the nail on the head’ means: describe exactly what is causing a problem.\"},{\"id\":\"q36\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ENIGMATIC’.\",\"options\":[\"energetic\",\"emphatic\",\"mysterious\",\"erratic\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘enigmatic’ means mysterious.\"},{\"id\":\"q37\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: She is capable ____ handling the pressure.\",\"options\":[\"of\",\"for\",\"at\",\"to\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Correct: She is capable of handling the pressure.\"},{\"id\":\"q38\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) Ten kilometres (B) are (C) a long distance (D) to walk.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"A distance as one amount: ‘is’.\"},{\"id\":\"q39\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who is easily deceived\",\"options\":[\"cynical\",\"vigilant\",\"sceptical\",\"gullible\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"A person who is easily deceived: gullible.\"},{\"id\":\"q40\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘cost an arm and a leg’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"need hard work\",\"cause an injury\",\"be cheap\",\"be very expensive\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘cost an arm and a leg’ means: be very expensive.\"},{\"id\":\"q41\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Choose the word closest in meaning to ‘ALLEVIATE’.\",\"options\":[\"allocate\",\"allude\",\"relieve\",\"alter\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"‘alleviate’ means relieve.\"},{\"id\":\"q42\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Fill in the blank: No sooner did she arrive ____ the lights went out.\",\"options\":[\"that\",\"than\",\"when\",\"then\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Correct: No sooner did she arrive than the lights went out.\"},{\"id\":\"q43\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Spot the part of the sentence that has an error:\\n(A) She (B) has (C) a lot of (D) knowledges.\",\"options\":[\"Part A\",\"Part B\",\"Part C\",\"Part D\",\"No error\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘Knowledge’ is uncountable: ‘knowledge’.\"},{\"id\":\"q44\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"One word for: A person who spends very little\",\"options\":[\"philanthropist\",\"miser\",\"spendthrift\",\"donor\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"A person who spends very little: miser.\"},{\"id\":\"q45\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What does the idiom ‘a drop in the ocean’ mean?\",\"options\":[\"a heavy rain\",\"a sea voyage\",\"a big mistake\",\"a very small amount compared to what is needed\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"‘a drop in the ocean’ means: a very small amount compared to what is needed.\"}]},{\"name\":\"Computer fundamentals\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q46\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What does ‘len([1, [2, 3], 4])’ return in Python?\",\"options\":[\"Error\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"The nested list counts as one element.\"},{\"id\":\"q47\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which device forwards frames using MAC addresses?\",\"options\":[\"Router\",\"Switch\",\"Modem\",\"Hub\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Switches work at layer 2.\"},{\"id\":\"q48\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"The difference between a process and a thread is that threads\",\"options\":[\"have separate address spaces\",\"always run on different machines\",\"share the memory of their process\",\"cannot run in parallel\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Threads of one process share its address space.\"},{\"id\":\"q49\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which scheduling algorithm can cause starvation of long jobs?\",\"options\":[\"First Come First Served\",\"Round Robin\",\"Shortest Job First\",\"Multilevel with ageing\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Short jobs keep jumping ahead.\"},{\"id\":\"q50\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Microservices architecture means\",\"options\":[\"an app built as small independently deployable services\",\"a database type\",\"only front-end code\",\"one large deployable unit\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Each service owns one capability.\"},{\"id\":\"q51\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which traversal uses a stack (explicitly or via recursion)?\",\"options\":[\"Depth-first search\",\"Level-order traversal\",\"Dijkstra with a queue\",\"Breadth-first search\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"DFS goes deep first.\"},{\"id\":\"q52\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"ACID properties of transactions are\",\"options\":[\"Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\",\"Accuracy, Concurrency, Integrity, Durability\",\"Atomicity, Concurrency, Isolation, Dependency\",\"Availability, Consistency, Isolation, Durability\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"Standard transaction guarantees.\"},{\"id\":\"q53\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which testing checks individual functions in isolation?\",\"options\":[\"System testing\",\"Acceptance testing\",\"Load testing\",\"Unit testing\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Smallest testable parts.\"},{\"id\":\"q54\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In MS Excel, which function adds a range of cells?\",\"options\":[\"TOTAL\",\"ADD\",\"SUM\",\"COUNT\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"=SUM(A1:A10).\"},{\"id\":\"q55\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Cloud model where you rent virtual machines and manage the OS yourself:\",\"options\":[\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\",\"FaaS\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Infrastructure as a Service.\"},{\"id\":\"q56\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Gmail is an example of\",\"options\":[\"On-premise software\",\"SaaS\",\"IaaS\",\"PaaS\"],\"answer\":1,\"explanation\":\"Software delivered over the internet.\"},{\"id\":\"q57\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"In C, the size of ‘char’ is\",\"options\":[\"2 bytes\",\"depends on the compiler always 8 bytes\",\"4 bytes\",\"1 byte\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"char is defined as one byte.\"},{\"id\":\"q58\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"What is a deadlock?\",\"options\":[\"Memory that cannot be freed\",\"A crashed disk\",\"A process that finishes early\",\"Processes waiting forever for resources held by each other\"],\"answer\":3,\"explanation\":\"Circular wait among processes.\"},{\"id\":\"q59\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"Which normal form removes partial dependencies on a composite key?\",\"options\":[\"2NF\",\"BCNF\",\"3NF\",\"1NF\"],\"answer\":0,\"explanation\":\"2NF requires full functional dependency on the whole key.\"},{\"id\":\"q60\",\"type\":\"MCQ\",\"text\":\"ARP is used to find\",\"options\":[\"the IP for a domain\",\"open ports\",\"the MAC address for an IP address\",\"the fastest route\"],\"answer\":2,\"explanation\":\"Address Resolution Protocol.\"}]}]}',1,'PRACTICE',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,0,1,1,NULL,'5f867bde-403b-454f-b2f0-6e569995f4f0','2026-11-23 19:03:07','2026-11-23 19:03:07'),('a926cf20-87fb-447e-8d60-056aa6b96420',NULL,'Infosys SP / DSE style · Coding','Three coding problems of rising difficulty in three hours. 3 coding problems in 180 minutes. Original practice questions modelled on the publicly reported test pattern. Not an official or past paper.','Infosys','HARD',14,180,3,3,30,'{\"title\":\"Infosys SP / DSE style · Coding\",\"description\":\"Three coding problems of rising difficulty in three hours. 3 coding problems in 180 minutes. Original practice questions modelled on the publicly reported test pattern. Not an official or past paper.\",\"companyTag\":\"Infosys\",\"level\":\"HARD\",\"order\":14,\"durationMinutes\":180,\"sections\":[{\"name\":\"Coding\",\"pick\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"q1\",\"type\":\"CODING\",\"title\":\"Coin change ways\",\"text\":\"Given coin values (unlimited supply of each) and an amount, print the number of ways to make the amount, modulo 1 000 000 007. Order of coins does not matter.\\n\\nInput: first line n and amount (1 ≤ n ≤ 100, 0 ≤ amount ≤ 10^4); second line n distinct coin values (1 to 10^4).\\nOutput: the number of ways mod 10^9+7.\",\"marks\":10,\"explanation\":\"Reference approach: see the standard technique for ‘Coin change ways’.\",\"starterCode\":{\"python\":\"import sys\\n\\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\\n# write your code here\\n\",\"java\":\"import java.util.*;\\nimport java.io.*;\\n\\npublic class Main {\\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\\n        // write your code here\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"cpp\":\"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nint main() {\\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\\n    // write your code here\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"javascript\":\"const data = require(\'fs\').readFileSync(0, \'utf8\').trim().split(/\\\\s+/);\\n// write your code here\\n\"},\"samples\":[{\"input\":\"3 5\\n1 2 5\\n\",\"output\":\"4\"},{\"input\":\"1 3\\n2\\n\",\"output\":\"0\"}],\"tests\":[{\"input\":\"2 0\\n3 7\\n\",\"output\":\"1\"},{\"input\":\"5 122\\n10 56 31 43 11\\n\",\"output\":\"5\"},{\"input\":\"13 2371\\n48 12 27 1 40 32 41 54 38 16 8 17 33\\n\",\"output\":\"618223956\"},{\"input\":\"14 311\\n26 4 44 32 35 20 33 6 5 50 58 46 53 17\\n\",\"output\":\"1982399\"},{\"input\":\"5 4136\\n29 23 2 42 33\\n\",\"output\":\"7014910\"},{\"input\":\"9 2128\\n8 14 52 48 33 25 29 49 3\\n\",\"output\":\"997044258\"},{\"input\":\"14 572\\n11 2 33 13 51 20 50 14 59 45 39 38 15 40\\n\",\"output\":\"372055308\"}]},{\"id\":\"q2\",\"type\":\"CODING\",\"title\":\"Running median\",\"text\":\"Numbers arrive one by one. After each one, print the median of all numbers so far; for an even count print the smaller of the two middle values.\\n\\nInput: first line n (1 ≤ n ≤ 10^5); second line n integers.\\nOutput: n medians separated by spaces.\",\"marks\":10,\"explanation\":\"Reference approach: see the standard technique for ‘Running median’.\",\"starterCode\":{\"python\":\"import sys\\n\\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\\n# write your code here\\n\",\"java\":\"import java.util.*;\\nimport java.io.*;\\n\\npublic class Main {\\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\\n        // write your code here\\n    }\\n}\\n\",\"cpp\":\"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nint main() {\\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\\n    // write your code here\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"javascript\":\"const data = require(\'fs\').readFileSync(0, \'utf8\').trim().split(/\\\\s+/);\\n// write your code here\\n\"},\"samples\":[{\"input\":\"5\\n5 15 1 3 8\\n\",\"output\":\"5 5 5 3 5\"},{\"input\":\"2\\n4 4\\n\",\"output\":\"4 4\"}],\"tests\":[{\"input\":\"1\\n-3\\n\",\"output\":\"-3\"},{\"input\":\"5189\\n-197519 -578250 -374082 935899 -177937 949224 -672382 -203199 297754 -65099 -648114 -24208 512882 511149 955824 -11510 -690282 985714 235914 -862397 -851112 -36055 186885 -272125 198022 -581299 653904 868647 114497 -161022 152667 -315342 222698 578021 -597111 143794 -106955 -226760 322494 -629114 -465219 -264726 -830053 -439579 -477844 -122400 -102909 276020 -942697 429334 -618927 665483 362853 -480313 347764 -222255 468945 423884 -14714 505573 -549837 -234133 -947361 773914 -877109 140730 710854 -144756 159928 364024 -768479 273190 658969 -867494 -133517 5